; pdf -- writing PDF files: a document of pages carrying text in the standard
; fonts, rules, filled rectangles and images, with named destinations and
; page labels. No font is embedded and no library needed: an image goes in
; as its file holds it, and the one that cannot -- a PNG with an alpha
; channel -- is decoded here. What is written is PDF 1.4.
;
; The modules, in dependency order: the width table of the standard fonts
; (generated), the fonts, the decoder, the document.

package scaly 0.1.0

define pdf
{
    module Metrics
    module Font
    module Inflate
    module Document
}
